From 2feb1e8a5e995c55705ab61091472d36d2ab5a0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hibreak <build@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:59:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Restore a no-op TelephonyMetrics for prebuilt IMS
 services

Android 16 removed com.android.internal.telephony.metrics.TelephonyMetrics.
MediaTek's ImsService (com.mediatek.ims, built for Android 14) still calls
TelephonyMetrics.getInstance() and writeOnRilSolicitedResponse(),
writeOnRilTimeoutResponse(), writeRilAnswer() and writeRilSendSms() from
its RIL adapter, so it dies with NoClassDefFoundError on the first IMS
RIL response.

Bring the class back with exactly those methods (plus the Android 10
writeRilSendSms signature that older MediaTek IMS builds use), all
no-ops. proguard.flags keeps public classes under
com.android.internal.telephony, so R8 leaves it in telephony-common.
---
 .../telephony/metrics/TelephonyMetrics.java   | 53 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 53 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/metrics/TelephonyMetrics.java

diff --git a/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/metrics/TelephonyMetrics.java b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/metrics/TelephonyMetrics.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7aaa971
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/metrics/TelephonyMetrics.java
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
